PROPOSAL ONLY (option B, yaw rate feedforward). Not applied; the owner decides
the new parameter and every value below. Values are the ones the model judged
(ffcommon.py / sweep.py, ens2.jsonl): P 0.65, I 0.07, FF per plant.

--- a/src/modules/airship_att_control/airship_att_control_params.yaml
+++ b/src/modules/airship_att_control/airship_att_control_params.yaml
@@ AS_YAWRATE_P
-      default: 0.5
+      default: 0.65
@@ AS_YAWRATE_I
-      default: 0.09
+      default: 0.07
@@ after AS_YR_INT_LIM
+    AS_YAWRATE_FF:
+      description:
+        short: Yaw rate feedforward
+        long: Normalized yaw torque per rad/s of commanded yaw rate, added to the
+          rate controller output. It supplies the torque that holds a commanded
+          rate against the hull's yaw damping, so the integrator holds less and
+          the vehicle stops sooner when the stick is released. Set it to the
+          torque that holds a steady turn divided by that turn rate (both
+          measured, torque in the unit of the yaw torque setpoint). Hull
+          damping grows with the square of the rate, so the value is right at
+          one rate only: too large overshoots and reverses on release at
+          smaller rates, too small leaves the rest to the integrator. 0 on a
+          vehicle without aerodynamic yaw damping. Unused where the yaw rate
+          loop stays open (see AS_YAWRATE_MAX).
+      type: float
+      default: 0.0
+      min: 0.0
+      max: 3.0
+      decimal: 3
+      increment: 0.01

--- a/src/modules/airship_att_control/airship_att_control.hpp
+++ b/src/modules/airship_att_control/airship_att_control.hpp
@@ DEFINE_PARAMETERS(
 		(ParamFloat<px4::params::AS_YAWRATE_I>) _param_as_yawrate_i,
+		(ParamFloat<px4::params::AS_YAWRATE_FF>) _param_as_yawrate_ff,
 		(ParamFloat<px4::params::AS_YR_INT_LIM>) _param_as_yr_int_lim,

--- a/src/modules/airship_att_control/airship_att_control_main.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/airship_att_control/airship_att_control_main.cpp
@@ AirshipAttitudeControl::parameters_updated()
 	_rate_control.setIntegratorLimit(Vector3f(0.f, 0.f, _param_as_yr_int_lim.get()));
+	// torque += FF * rate setpoint (rate_control.cpp:78); only yaw has a loop
+	_rate_control.setFeedForwardGain(Vector3f(0.f, 0.f, _param_as_yawrate_ff.get()));
 	_yaw_rate_max = math::radians(_param_as_yawrate_max.get());

Airframe defaults, one per gz physics variant (the value is a property of the
plant, not of the vehicle's controller):

--- a/ROMFS/px4fmu_common/init.d-posix/airframes/2527_gz_airship_vectored_independent_am_fin_drag
+++ b/ROMFS/px4fmu_common/init.d-posix/airframes/2527_gz_airship_vectored_independent_am_fin_drag
 . ${R}etc/init.d-posix/airframes/2520_gz_airship_vectored_independent
